{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Zevach</b> — shelamim." "<b>And minchah</b> — in the marcheshet and machavat. And the meaning: for Your thoughts are to do good toward us, not in exchange for payments. And behold, after zevach and minchah he mentioned olah and chatat. Rabbi Moses said: for the word לא חפצת serves on account of what follows, and the meaning is: You did not make heard such as this in my ears, when You spoke with me at Mount Sinai. And what is correct in my eyes: You did not request zevach, only You formed ears for me, that I might hearken to Your voice, as in: \"Behold, to obey is better than zevach.\" (n: Ibn Ezra reads הנה שמוע מזבח טוב from 1 Samuel 15:22, citing it in its Hebrew form with the phrase \"to obey\" rendered as שמוע.)"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:24.556959387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}